<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#ankole-watusi">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ankole-Watusi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ankole-Watusi is a breed of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> known for its enormous horns, developed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in the twentieth century from long-horned Sanga cattle of east-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Its ancestors include the Ankole cattle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahima">Bahima</a> herders of Nkore in Uganda and the long-horned cattle of Rwanda and Burundi. In Nkore itself the long-horned herds were the chief measure of wealth and status and the basis of the Bahima diet of milk and butter.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ankole-watusi.jpg" alt="Ankole-Watusi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dennis G. Jarvis · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ankole-Watusi,_Cambridge,_Ontario_(14656696757),_cropped.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
